{"name":"Ho Chi Minh City","slug":"ho-chi-minh-city","region":"Southeast Asia & Oceania","lat":10.82,"lon":106.63,"seasons":{"DJF":{"season_name":"Dec 2026–Feb 2027","years":[1951,1952,1953,1954,1955,1956,1957,1958,1959,1960,1961,1962,1963,1964,1965,1966,1967,1968,1969,1970,1971,1972,1973,1974,1975,1976,1977,1978,1979,1980,1981,1982,1983,1984,1985,1986,1987,1988,1989,1990,1991,1992,1993,1994,1995,1996,1997,1998,1999,2000,2001,2002,2003,2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025],"roni_lead":[-0.38,0.98,0.04,0.84,-0.31,-1.31,-0.14,1.16,0.24,0.04,0.08,-0.16,-0.3,1.06,-0.64,1.86,-0.03,-0.08,0.56,0.67,-0.57,-0.4,1.82,-1.63,-0.45,-0.95,1.04,0.89,-0.08,0.52,-0.06,-0.17,2.03,-0.9,-0.61,-0.18,1.0,1.2,-1.71,-0.23,0.27,1.2,0.1,0.46,0.97,-0.93,-0.25,2.22,-1.33,-1.06,-0.55,-0.18,1.18,0.17,0.7,-0.18,0.73,-1.33,-0.38,0.86,-1.61,-0.91,0.21,-0.22,0.35,2.03,-0.96,-0.82,0.62,0.15,-1.37,-1.08,-1.1,1.3,-0.76],"paragraph":"Dec–Feb in Ho Chi Minh City has warmed by about 0.25 °C per decade since 1951, roughly 1.8 °C in all, with the coldest days warming fastest, so cold extremes are becoming rarer. There is a strong, well-established El Niño effect on temperature: after El Niño conditions in the preceding fall, Dec–Feb tends to run warmer, and El Niño accounts for about 35% of the year-to-year ups and downs. With this year's strong El Niño, that push is about 2 times a normal year-to-year swing, roughly as much warmth as 35 years of the long-term trend. Without El Niño, a Dec–Feb this warm would come about once every 27 years. El Niño moves the coldest days most: this season they are expected to shift by about 1.4 °C, against 0.6 °C for the hottest days. Dec–Feb rainfall has risen by about 5% per decade. El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a drier season with fewer rainy days, and this year's shift is substantial. Humidity shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a less humid Dec–Feb, and this year's shift is substantial. For Dec 2026–Feb 2027, a warmer-than-normal season is very likely (more than 95% chance), about 1.3 °C above the 1991–2020 average; a less humid season than normal is more likely than not (about 55%). This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":26.7427,"trend_per_decade":0.2452,"trend_p":0.0,"trend_total_since_1951":1.8391,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.3919,"enso_p":0.0,"confidence":"Strong","survives_fdr":true,"fraction_explained":0.3668,"intrinsic_sd":0.4826,"effect_this_season":0.8622,"effect_ratio":1.7865,"size":"Dominant","size_typical_el_nino":"Dominant","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":27.0,"expected_anomaly_2027":1.3393,"p_below":0.0008,"p_near":0.013,"p_above":0.9862,"forecast_words":"Very likely (>95%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":true,"years_of_warming_equivalent":35.1604,"values":[25.884,26.349,26.201,25.931,25.589,25.227,25.17,26.291,26.011,25.843,25.659,25.301,24.461,26.705,24.828,26.805,25.107,25.242,26.619,25.699,25.337,25.375,26.719,25.06,26.188,24.526,25.762,26.623,26.413,26.132,25.948,25.536,26.345,25.765,26.568,25.174,26.229,26.528,26.221,26.649,26.891,26.575,26.045,26.289,26.63,25.68,25.932,28.087,26.319,26.353,26.569,27.122,27.172,26.669,26.571,26.421,26.831,26.967,25.939,27.186,26.423,26.828,27.819,25.924,26.28,27.888,27.122,26.902,27.708,27.14,26.298,27.347,26.579,27.827,26.684],"forecast_mean":28.082,"forecast_sd":0.5259,"fit":{"a2027":27.2199,"b":0.3919,"c":0.0245,"tercile_low":26.4227,"tercile_high":26.9233},"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.2881,"trend_p":0.0,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.6282,"enso_p":0.0,"confidence":"Strong","shift_this_season":1.3821,"lines_cross":false},"p50":{"trend_per_decade":0.2526,"trend_p":0.0,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.3886,"enso_p":0.0,"confidence":"Strong","shift_this_season":0.8548,"lines_cro